[110.346058, "o", "=== PASSAGE_0012 ===\r\n4 CONTRAINDICATIONS\r\nPAXLOVID is contraindicated in patients with a history of clinically significant hypersensitivity reactions e.g., toxic epidermal necrolysis (TEN) or Stevens-Johnson syndrome] to its active ingredients (nirmatrelvir or ritonavir) or any other components of the product.\r\nPAXLOVID i...\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0013 ===\r\n5.1\tRisk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions\r\nInitiation of PAXLOVID, which contains ritonavir, a strong CYP3A inhibitor, in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A or initiation of medications metabolized by CYP3A in patients already receiving PAXLOVID, may increase pla...\r\n\r\n"]
[110.346092, "o", "=== PASSAGE_0019 ===\r\n7.1\tPotential for PAXLOVID to Affect Other Drugs\r\nPAXLOVID (nirmatrelvir co-packaged with ritonavir) is a strong inhibitor of CYP3A, and an inhibitor of CYP2D6, P-gp and OATP1B1. Co-administration of PAXLOVID with drugs that are primarily metabolized by CYP3A and CYP2D6 or are transported by P-gp or ...\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0021 ===\r\n7.3\tEstablished and Other Potentially Significant Drug Interactions\r\nTable 2 provides a listing of clinically significant drug interactions, including contraindicated drugs . Drugs listed in Table 2 are a guide and not considered a comprehensive list of all possible drugs that may interact with PAXLO...\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0022 ===\r\n↑ alfuzosin\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential hypotension ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0024 ===\r\n↑ ranolazine\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious and/or life-threatening reactions ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0025 ===\r\n↑ antiarrhythmic\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for cardiac arrhythmias ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0027 ===\r\n↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance ....\r\n"]
[110.34631, "o", "\r\n=== PASSAGE_0034 ===\r\n↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0041 ===\r\n↑ colchicine\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious and/or life-threatening reactions in patients with renal and/or hepatic impairment ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0045 ===\r\n↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance. Alternate antimycobacterial drugs such as rifabutin should be considered ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0048 ===\r\n↑ lurasidone↑ pimozide\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to serious and/or life-threatening reactions such as cardiac arrhythmias ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0051 ===\r\n↑ silodosin\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for postural hypotension ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0054 ===\r\n↑ eplerenone\r\nCo-administration with eplerenone is contraindicated due to potential for hyperkalemia ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0055 ===\r\n"]
[110.34636, "o", "↑ ivabradine\r\nCo-administration with ivabradine is contraindicated due to potential for bradycardia or conduction disturbances ....\r\n"]
[110.346424, "o", "\r\n=== PASSAGE_0059 ===\r\n↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0063 ===\r\n↑ dihydroergotamine↑ ergotamine↑ methylergonovine\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for acute ergot toxicity characterized by vasospasm and ischemia of the extremities and other tissues including the central nervous system ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0068 ===\r\n↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0069 ===\r\n↑ lovastatin↑ simvastatin\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for myopathy including rhabdomyolysis .\r\nIf treatment with PAXLOVID is considered medically necessary, discontinue use of lovastatin and simvastatin at least 12 hours prior to initiation of PAXLOVID, during the 5 days of PAX...\r\n"]
[110.346447, "o", "\r\n=== PASSAGE_0072 ===\r\n↑ voclosporin\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for acute and/or chronic nephrotoxicity ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0079 ===\r\n↑ lomitapide\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for hepatotoxicity and gastrointestinal adverse reactions ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0080 ===\r\n↑ eletriptan\r\nCo-administration of eletriptan within at least 72 hours of PAXLOVID is contraindicated due to potential for serious adverse reactions including cardiovascular and cerebrovascular events ....\r\n"]
[110.346465, "o", "\r\n=== PASSAGE_0081 ===\r\n"]
[110.346543, "o", "↑ ubrogepant\r\nCo-administration of ubrogepant with PAXLOVID is contraindicated due to potential for serious adverse reactions ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0083 ===\r\n↑ finerenone\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious adverse reactions including hyperkalemia, hypotension, and hyponatremia ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0089 ===\r\n↑ naloxegol\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to the potential for opioid withdrawal symptoms ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0090 ===\r\n↑ sildenafil\r\nCo-administration of sildenafil with PAXLOVID is contraindicated for use in pulmonary hypertension due to the potential for sildenafil associated adverse events, including visual abnormalities hypotension, prolonged erection, and syncope ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0095 ===\r\n↑ triazolam↑ midazolam\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for extreme sedation and respiratory depression ....\r\n\r\n=== PASSAGE_0098 ===\r\n"]
[110.346662, "o", "↑ flibanserin\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for hypotension, syncope, and CNS depression ....\r\n\r\n"]
[110.346717, "o", "=== PASSAGE_0099 ===\r\n↑ tolvaptan\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for dehydration, hypovolemia and hyperkalemia ....\r\n\r\n"]
